&lt;p&gt;Ready to shape the future of talent acquisition in a global trading firm? As a Senior Campus Recruiter, you&#39;ll be the driving force behind spotting and bringing the top 1% of talent from Europe&#39;s premier universities on board. Your journey involves navigating the full campus recruitment lifecycle, from identification to selection, and making your mark at European recruitment events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll join our Campus Recruitment team in Europe, based in Amsterdam, part of a wider recruitment organisation of experienced tech, trading and business support recruiters. Collaboration comes first here: we share knowledge, step in for each other in peak season, and succeed as one team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end recruitment process: screening, interviewing, assessment review, offer conversations and closing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong partnerships with business leaders and interviewers, and make sure we&#39;re aligned on hiring needs and on what great looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a data-driven way, using insights to make our process sharper, fairer and more efficient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to strategic projects such as market analyses, process and assessment reviews, and improvements to how we select&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent IMC at recruitment events across Europe, with frequent travel (more than four times a year)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we look for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of industry experience, ideally within a global finance, trading, tech or consultancy organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of financial markets and the trading industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A critical eye: you question how things are done, spot trends early and turn them into practical improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to think strategically and act tactically, moving easily between the bigger picture and getting things done today&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solution-oriented mindset: when something isn&#39;t working, you look for a better way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy operational recruitment. Running a tight process and giving candidates a great experience energises you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build relationships with the business with ease and earn trust as a partner, not just a service provider&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in a dynamic environment where no two days are the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well in a larger team and put collaboration first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You keep up with industry trends and best practices in campus recruitment and bring them into your own work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A unique work culture that values collaboration, initiative, and ownership. Our professional and friendly environment provides the perfect backdrop for your growth and responsibilities. We operate with transparency in a flat structure, allowing you direct engagement with stakeholders and professionals. Your input matters here, contributing to our collective success. At IMC, continuous learning is a priority. Various training and on-the-job growth opportunities allow you to shape your path within the organisation. This isn&#39;t just a job; it&#39;s a journey of ongoing growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We appreciate your efforts. Our highly competitive salary comes with great perks. If you&#39;re looking for a friendly yet professional space to contribute and grow, IMC is the place. If you&#39;re ready for a role beyond routine recruitment, where your experience can contribute to the future of our team and company, apply now.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;IMC is a research-driven trading firm where quantitative modeling, machine learning, and engineering shape how modern markets are traded. A stabilizing force in markets since 1989, we provide liquidity across trading venues, delivering the best outcome in value and risk management to investors. Using our own technology and capital, we build proprietary systems and algorithms that operate across global markets. Our researchers, traders, and engineers work as a collective, combining rapid experimentation, advanced infrastructure, and real-time feedback to turn insight into execution and execution into advantage.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Are you comfortable navigating complex software systems, working with coding agents, and defining what makes developer tools actually useful? Do you want to shape how developers and AI work together inside IDEs?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About JetBrains&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create intelligent software development tools for developers and teams. More than 15 million users, over 300,000 companies, and 88 of the Fortune Global Top 100 rely on our products to solve real, complex problems. Our mission is simple: make development teams more productive and AI adoptable at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agentic development is changing how software gets built. Developers no longer just chat with AI – they delegate tasks, run parallel agent sessions, and steer autonomous changes. As agents take on more work, reviewing and owning the output is becoming the hardest part of the process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JetBrains Air is our open system for agentic development. It brings tools like Codex, GitHub Copilot, Claude Agent, Gemini, and Junie directly into JetBrains IDEs, providing an agentic-first user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Product Manager to lead key areas of Air. You’ll take ownership of high-impact workflows, work closely with cross-functional teams (including software engineers, designers, ML researchers, analysts, DevRel, and product marketing), and turn technical complexity into clear product direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end ownership of key parts of Air in JetBrains IDEs, driving work from problem framing and discovery to delivery, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and refine core agentic workflows, including task delegation, session monitoring, steering, and code review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model complex user flows, system states, permissions, and integration schemes to guide engineering and design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a transparent roadmap that balances quick improvements with long-term strategic investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define telemetry, design experiments, analyze product data, and make evidence-based roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Study how developers interact with leading AI agents and tools to inform product priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with the Agent Client Protocol (ACP) ecosystem and collaborate with partners building on it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with enterprise sales and support teams to address governance, privacy, and control requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems-thinking mindset that easily breaks down complex architectures, workflows, and dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven approach to product decisions, including hands-on experience querying and analyzing telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active personal experience using coding agents and clear perspectives on where current AI tools succeed and fail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product intuition for complex technical user experiences and developer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise, and collaborative communication skills with the ability to explain complex technical concepts simply and build alignment across diverse groups of stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort navigating fast-changing technical landscapes with high ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience shipping end-user products as a product manager or in a similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical grounding in software development workflows, including IDEs, git, code review, CI/CD, and package management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on technical background sufficient to collaborate closely with software and ML engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of core AI and agent concepts, including tool use, protocols (MCP/ACP), context retrieval, evaluations, and latency/cost trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to write SQL or Python to analyze product metrics and experiment results independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English, both written and spoken.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first 6 to 12 months, success in this role means:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving measurable growth in active Air users and improving weekly/monthly retention (D7/D30).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increasing agent session completion rates and the proportion of agent-generated changes accepted by developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishing clear, telemetry-backed decisions across your product roadmap areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivering validated product hypotheses consistently each quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing directly to JetBrains AI revenue growth and overall IDE value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join JetBrains?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong base salary – We offer competitive pay that reflects your skills and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work schedule – Enjoy the freedom to work from home or from the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra time off – More days to relax, recharge, and do the things you love.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities – Access to conferences, courses, and language classes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free meals and snacks – Lunch and refreshments provided to keep you fueled.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health and wellness – On-site gyms or sports club stipends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal events – Company-wide celebrations and team gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer. We know great ideas can come from anyone, anywhere. That’s why we do our best to create an open and inclusive workplace – one that welcomes everyone regardless of their background, identity, religion, age, accessibility needs, or orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like a challenge you&#39;d enjoy, send us your resume and a short note on why you&#39;re interested in Air.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-KL1&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We know great ideas can come from anyone, anywhere. That’s why we do our best to create an open and inclusive workplace – one that welcomes everyone regardless of their background, identity, religion, age, accessibility needs, or orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;We process the data provided in your job application in accordance with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.jetbrains.com/legal/docs/privacy/privacy-recruitment/&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;(FEQ128R42)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the technical leader and lead architect for one of Databricks&#39; most strategic global customers: a health technology company whose diagnostic, therapy, connected-care and consumer health products reach hundreds of millions of people every year. You will own the technical relationship and the Data + AI vision for a single complex enterprise that spans multiple business units, regions and regulatory regimes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The account is a large, Azure-first Data Intelligence Platform customer. It runs a portfolio of well over a hundred use cases across business units and global functions, delivered as a multi-year program in quarterly releases. You will set the technical direction for that program and turn it into an executable roadmap. You will work as one team with the Account Executive and a dedicated pod of Solutions Architects, specialists, Professional Services and partners. We are looking for a visionary who can see where Data + AI will take health technology, explain that clearly to executives and engineers alike, and bring a large, distributed group of people with them!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Impact You Will Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own and drive the technical vision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the customer&#39;s enterprise Data + AI vision with CxO and VP stakeholders, tied directly to business priorities. Be the executive suite&#39;s trusted advisor on platform strategy, build-vs-buy, responsible AI and regulated-industry governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show, don&#39;t tell: inspire CTOs, chief architects and engineering leaders with working examples, and build prototypes yourself when it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the account pod technically: set direction for Solutions Architects, Specialist and Delivery SAs, Professional Services and partners, and coach them to raise the bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Account Executive on account strategy and consumption planning, owning technical strategy and path to value for every major initiative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align pre-sales, delivery and partners so the customer sees one Databricks team, one plan and one escalation path, local to global. Lead discovery and solution design for strategic, high-risk deployments, driving each to production and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build lasting C-level, VP and Director relationships across IT, data &amp;amp; AI, R&amp;amp;D, Quality &amp;amp; Regulatory, Service, Operations and the business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the customer&#39;s voice internally, shaping Databricks product and go-to-market strategy with field insight while leading the account&#39;s largest modernisation programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale GenAI and agentic AI from pilot to production across business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build partner ecosystem relationships (GSIs, ISVs, hyperscalers) to scale delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create reusable IP (reference designs, accelerators, talks, blogs) for the wider Databricks health and life sciences community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;(Note: it is not expected that you “tick every box” below and encourage you to apply if you are meeting several of the key criteria and can demonstrate a strong ability to transfer skills and develop quickly in the role!) &amp;nbsp; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven record as lead technical figure on a large global enterprise account, or as enterprise/chief architect at a similar organisation, owning the vision over multiple years.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading virtual teams without direct authority: setting direction, coaching senior architects and aligning specialists, delivery and partners on one plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives with high autonomy in ambiguous, high-stakes, multi-region, multi-business-unit environments. Excellent communicator, from boardroom to engineering floor, with clear written thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical depth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in data engineering, analytics, ML or AI architecture, with significant customer-facing technical leadership (pre-sales, consulting or enterprise architecture).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, hands-on expertise in modern data and AI platforms; Apache Spark, Delta Lake and Databricks experience is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Large-scale data platforms and migrations from legacy warehouses, Hadoop or other clouds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise governance and security models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production ML, MLOps, GenAI and agent systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to win platform decisions against hyperscaler-native and competing platforms on architecture, cost and governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Python and SQL; able to prototype quickly, including with AI-assisted development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in health technology, medical devices, life sciences or another regulated industry, and a passion for improving patient outcomes with Data + AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of MedTech and medical AI regulation:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU MDR/IVDR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FDA SaMD and Predetermined Change Control Plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ISO 13485, IEC 62304 and ISO 14971&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU AI Act requirements for high-risk medical AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of privacy and data-sharing regimes (GDPR, HIPAA, European Health Data Space). Familiarity with healthcare data standards (DICOM, HL7, FHIR, OMOP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with or at a global MedTech, health technology or diagnostics company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing validated, audit-ready (GxP / 21 CFR Part 11) data and AI environments. Enterprise-scale SAP data integration (BW, S/4HANA) and semantic harmonisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public thought leadership: conference talks, publications or open source.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dutch is a plus; professional English required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Databricks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Databricks is the Data and AI company. More than 20,000 organizations worldwide — including adidas, AT&amp;amp;T, Bayer, Block, Mastercard, Rivian, Unilever, and 70% of the Fortune 500 — rely on the Databricks Data + AI Platform to build and scale data and AI apps, analytics and agents. Headquartered in San Francisco with 30+ offices around the globe, Databricks offers a unified platform that includes Genie, Lakebase, Agent Bricks, Lakeflow, Lakehouse, and Unity Catalog. To learn more, follow Databricks on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/databricks&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://x.com/databricks&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/@Databricks&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/databricksinc/?hl=en&quot;&gt;Instagram&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;At Databricks, we strive to provide comprehensive benefits and perks that meet the needs of all of our employees. For specific details on the benefits offered in your region click &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/154un3e8Xav4BceOSlcYFZRGEuQI54xMxVydRwQn54eQ/edit?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Databricks, we are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive culture where everyone can excel. We take great care to ensure that our hiring practices are inclusive and meet equal employment opportunity standards. Individuals looking for employment at Databricks are considered without regard to age, color, disability, ethnicity, family or marital status, gender identity or expression, language, national origin, physical and mental ability, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, socio-economic status, veteran status, and other protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If access to export-controlled technology or source code is required for performance of job duties, it is within Employer&#39;s discretion whether to apply for a U.S. government license for such positions, and Employer may decline to proceed with an applicant on this basis alone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;SLSQ427R122&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Want to help solve the world&#39;s toughest problems with data and AI? This is what we do every day at Databricks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Databricks operates at the leading edge of the Data and AI space. Our customers rely on us to drive the accelerated innovation needed to stay ahead in today’s highly competitive landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Named Enterprise Hunter Account Executive to join the team to maximise the phenomenal market opportunity that exists for Databricks across Benelux. Reporting to the Director of Enterprise Sales, you will be responsible for driving strategic growth and expanding our footprint across the region’s most critical enterprise accounts. This role is hybrid, based in Amsterdam.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The impact you will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess your list of assigned accounts and develop a strategy to execute against it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a customer base, identifying and closing new logo opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead your customers and partners to identify impactful big data and AI use cases whilst proving out their value on the Databricks Lakehouse platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify land opportunities and develop the expand / consumption use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate and utilise internal teams to maximise the impact on your ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build exceptional value with all engagements to guide successful negotiations to close point&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What we look for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 4+ years of experience selling SaaS solutions to Enterprise Customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience and strong performance in new logo hunting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Big Data, Cloud, or SaaS industries with some technical sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful experience selling complex software deals and quota over-achievement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of consumption based land and expand sales models is advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the Data &amp;amp; AI space with some technology sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of creating demand that delivered substantial business value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of following robust sales methodologies and process, e.g. account planning, MEDDPICC, Value Selling and accurate forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of building effective champions, collaborative teams and partnerships to support execution of your territory plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how to identify all key uses cases and buying centres in an opportunity to increase the impact of Databricks in an organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the Benelux territory and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in business English and Dutch&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
